# ── Public-repo boundary (SPEC: Security & Privacy) — never commit ──────────
# Patterns are anchored where needed: ziggurat/data/ is the (public) ingestion
# package; only the top-level intel/ and data/ trees are league-private.
/intel/
/data/
# Trailing-wildcard on purpose (item 3.2c): the anchored forms below matched
# neither a backup named ziggurat.sqlite.bak-v7 nor ziggurat.sqlite.gz, and
# repo_guard.py's pattern was anchored the same way — so a 43 MB file of
# league-private data cleared TWO of the three enforcement points Rule 5 names.
*.sqlite*
*.sqlite3*
.env
.env.*

# ── Python ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage*
htmlcov/

# ── Local tooling ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.claude/settings.local.json
.DS_Store
